edb/ref 17592186304676}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3c782024-64b0-58c7-9205-ffc4beaa0f2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-332634" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-2x(t)+4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=x(t)-y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. Find equations of the $x$- and $y$-nullclines for the corresponding phase space.\n\n$\\,$\nThe $x$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-1}}. \n\n$\\,$\nThe $y$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Recall that: \n\n- The $x$-nullcline is a line for which ${x}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are vertical). So, to find it, we set the first equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n-2x+4y=0\\,⇒\\,y=\\frac{1}{2}x\n$$\n\n- The $y$-nullcline is a line for which ${y}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are horizontal). So, to find it, we set the second equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\nx-y=0\\,⇒\\,y=x\n$$\n\nPlotting these in the phase space, we obtain the following:\n\n![](images/19/19c33a634af36765142e2f4b85df1b9209d3f1abf105a131b629b3249bd91c2c.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391010 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166910 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d219270-5202-54e6-8cba-dc816155bd7b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Nullclines of a System of Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ffb971ce-3049-51fe-a2a9-c6213cc2efee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391012} {:answer/id #uuid "bf670add-7944-52cc-b5a3-85e4e4a604c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391013} {:answer/id #uuid "bb4b7a2a-e2e0-587f-89c2-2aaafeb3f74e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391014} {:answer/id #uuid "99569669-a543-5340-987b-9fc9931edc10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391015}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf670add-7944-52cc-b5a3-85e4e4a604c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391013} :answer-field/id #uuid "61a88848-0820-56d5-8abf-a85a11640c85" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391011} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a44db6a6-2316-5d2c-8d64-0db34ccee926" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391017} {:answer/id #uuid "d2157be3-cbfc-59ce-9f32-0279b2cb490e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391018} {:answer/id #uuid "0fd45b74-ec56-5bae-afc9-e9351e6d106e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391019} {:answer/id #uuid "d74c784d-bc11-5a4e-81c2-e3b3a5111808" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391020}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d74c784d-bc11-5a4e-81c2-e3b3a5111808" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391020} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1143ad8-a7c5-5043-8f31-4c5191cbed01" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391016}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5e7fabf8-a5ca-5309-a7c3-5690ee882dd5" :question/math-academy-id "q-332651" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-3x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=5x(t)+y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. Find equations of the $x$- and $y$-nullclines for the corresponding phase space.\n\n$\\,$\nThe $x$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-1}}. \n\n$\\,$\nThe $y$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Recall that: \n\n- The $x$-nullcline is a line for which ${x}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are vertical). So, to find it, we set the first equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n-3x+y=0\\,⇒\\,y=3x\n$$\n\n- The $y$-nullcline is a line for which ${y}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are horizontal). So, to find it, we set the second equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n5x+y=0\\,⇒\\,y=-5x\n$$\n\nPlotting these in the phase space, we obtain the following:\n\n![](images/c5/c5bbfde035449e1495b02d71a2b1199bf0dbaf7388e0c8eefa1e40e0816fdf7a.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391103 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166911 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "129bee33-7c18-5450-affe-dd710a3a75dd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Trajectory Given a Starting Point and the Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65f927a4-1b64-540f-bb7c-e15e61482db1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/80/80d758f23c0962d0611fca95f5ce5e7654346f133ceb7cf1275aaf3071ed1838.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391105} {:answer/id #uuid "fda175e8-b02e-5fd6-b042-504a1948f51a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0f/0f513a1fb254df7d6a6aaaa13632a0312b5483b622bcc83a154b4e80bd392a42.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391106} {:answer/id #uuid "d2e13b20-d127-5c45-9a52-5a283c7618b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e3/e3b4b7001ce149759e4356b594dace06641e815860d33a6e2a2b3143078b58fa.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391107} {:answer/id #uuid "ab1c6572-7c67-5521-8482-c910338dc838" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c1/c1517d81fb17366779bf77a0608f5f8d691f302d009d0f677a6ca0c6c02cd527.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391108} {:answer/id #uuid "03b7217f-4a6f-50f5-982b-e1649d39aa5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f4/f49c17becabf4088e886ddfc8e086c81184d94e6637c44458205c47410be1a3d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391109}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65f927a4-1b64-540f-bb7c-e15e61482db1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/80/80d758f23c0962d0611fca95f5ce5e7654346f133ceb7cf1275aaf3071ed1838.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391105} :answer-field/id #uuid "829923eb-1895-5bc9-8cd1-365ba2040166" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391104}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d9ff10b6-480b-50d2-b813-5532190d7591" :question/math-academy-id "q-332837" :question/problem "![](images/97/9703f99ca670b5924bf668fc77bcc09d8be652487259b0ea8753fc38c85d7013.png)\n\nA sketch of the phase space with nullclines and the corresponding direction field of tangents to the solutions of a system of differential equations is shown above (the tangents are not drawn to scale). Which of the following could represent the trajectory starting at the point marked on the graph?" :question/worked-solution "Let's sketch the trajectory.\n\n- We start at the given point and go along with the flow (downward and to the right) until the trajectory intersects the $y$-nullcline, where the tangents are horizontal.\n\n![](images/7f/7f98b4ad206556ac8a7c8eae16d216af9d91a375907e3fd058247e70195e1669.png)\n\n- After that, the trajectory continues going to the right and slightly upward to infinity.\n\n![](images/3b/3ba48b118f4ed24dcf6866579fae201af0b36252e537ab99ac2b87e08a889e15.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308342 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166911 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "129bee33-7c18-5450-affe-dd710a3a75dd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Trajectory Given a Starting Point and the Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61df7f22-6ffa-57a8-9916-b16cd0e6d7a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7d/7d6d07e888cd0dd55fd37a8a620c8be054eee0e6abc170133a4188667dcc65b4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306098} {:answer/id #uuid "7e88af57-d11c-5f11-ae26-c363739c22eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6e/6e2e7d099ed478a259b241320481c4beacda56cea59adc2c7314636f42e79f3e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306363} {:answer/id #uuid "9713628a-50bc-55aa-9c55-eaff442a58c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0e/0eff17334f3ca56152140bfefaf10a3169ad34a8b6e1e3322bd7fb03963c2338.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306572} {:answer/id #uuid "be682b22-dd95-5509-aae0-426f78a07495" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f1/f128b9d7ed44f4b0e7c40177e7198c0593f6ff9b262fae153ffbfad963d00873.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306926} {:answer/id #uuid "c90626e8-1636-5700-ba43-5e845dd15842" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f9/f906ea39089da431a1b86d3e7b8ab68ff7a287f8c4af4c3a5b9c1117eff2b57b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307022}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9713628a-50bc-55aa-9c55-eaff442a58c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0e/0eff17334f3ca56152140bfefaf10a3169ad34a8b6e1e3322bd7fb03963c2338.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306572} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8399834-d23a-59a9-8ff6-060b534eecb5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308106}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2dfbad27-2f3a-51d2-ab57-9054aa8268d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-332932" :question/problem "![](images/83/83147b64f8f34d43b9503186f3d2df5926ce119953c80d10f4cd8b8ef94bfcfc.png)\n\nA sketch of the phase space with nullclines and the corresponding direction field of tangents to the solutions of a system of differential equations is shown above (the tangents are not drawn to scale). Which of the following could represent the trajectory starting at the point marked on the graph?" :question/worked-solution "Let's sketch the trajectory.\n\n- We start at the given point, going along with the flow (upward and slightly to the right) until the trajectory intersects the $x$-nullcline, where the tangents are vertical.\n\n![](images/6d/6d897c2e9249447cc2d0c902a592d04442b0928c315163b6ab80cff288c84657.png)\n\n- Next, the flow continues going upward but then starts turning  to the left.\n\n![](images/be/bed6896ecc0edcdb157b648108d403e1b8e29463d9f61aa0e0c26e8f5e2dd8c6.png)\n\n- After that, the trajectory continues upward and slightly to the left, suggesting that it may converge to the origin\n\n![](images/cc/cc53577a278595e5f0155119aa5eb1a7b27ec01847a6daa1ba6ade6792c5f5e9.png)"}]}
